6. Active Directory User Management

Active Directory Users and Computers (ADUC) can be used to create and manage domain user accounts and group memberships when the administrator has the appropriate permissions.

6.1 Creating a User

Basic workflow:

Active Directory Users and Computers
        ↓
Select appropriate OU
        ↓
New
        ↓
User
        ↓
Enter user information
        ↓
Set password
        ↓
Apply company password policy
        ↓
Create account

A temporary password can be assigned and the user can be required to change it at their next logon, depending on organizational policy.

7. Active Directory Group Membership

Security groups allow administrators to organize accounts into manageable units and commonly provide access to resources through group membership.

Basic Workflow
User
 ↓
Properties
 ↓
Member Of
 ↓
Add
 ↓
Select Security Group
 ↓
Apply
Why use Security Groups?

Instead of assigning permissions individually to every user, permissions can be assigned to a group and users can receive access through their group membership.

Example
Finance Security Group
        ↓
Finance Shared Folder Permission
        ↓
Finance Users

This improves consistency and reduces administrative effort.

8. Active Directory Password Reset

Basic Help Desk workflow:

Verify user's identity
        ↓
Locate user in ADUC
        ↓
Reset Password
        ↓
Set temporary password
        ↓
Require password change if company policy requires
        ↓
User attempts login
        ↓
Verify
        ↓
Document

Microsoft's ADUC workflow supports resetting passwords and can also provide an option to unlock a locked account during the password-reset process.

9. Locked vs Disabled Accounts
Locked Account

A locked account is temporarily prevented from authenticating, commonly because the account-lockout policy was triggered after repeated failed authentication attempts.

Help Desk workflow
Verify user identity
        ↓
Check account status
        ↓
Unlock account if authorized
        ↓
Verify login
        ↓
Document

If the account becomes locked again, investigate the underlying cause rather than repeatedly unlocking it.

Disabled Account

A disabled account still exists in Active Directory but is prevented from new sign-ins.

An administrator can disable or enable the account through ADUC.

Important distinction
Locked
↓
Authentication temporarily blocked

Disabled
↓
Account intentionally disabled

Deleted
↓
Account removed from Active Directory
